LR-TDDFT HF on H2O, gamma_only, nspin=2, lr_nstates=2, lr_solver=dav.
Retains Z-CG coverage. abs_gauge=none skips optical postprocessing.

LR eigenvector accuracy (2026-10-29)
----------------------------------
The signed force components and their absolute-value sum retain their original
1e-6 eV/Angstrom limits. The former lr_thr=1e-2 reference recorded an
approximate Davidson state: changing its expansion/stopping path changes
forces well beyond these limits. Use lr_thr=1e-16 to resolve the eigenvectors
for this small LR problem, retaining lr_solver=dav and the original basis
size, iteration budget, ground-state SCF settings and Z-CG solver.

References come from dense LAPACK diagonalization in upstream c82d87d9e,
using the same physical inputs and ground-state settings. Upstream and
current LAPACK give identical printed signed force components; the accurate
current Davidson result agrees in every component and in the force sum to
within 2e-7 eV/Angstrom. The tighter request uses the existing
retry policy and produces no final nonconvergence warning. The lr_thr value is an
eigenvalue-change request, not a claim that the residual equals 1e-16.

Calibration uses GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, Libxc 7.0.0 with KXC enabled,
four MPI ranks and one OpenMP/BLAS thread. Both the signed table and scalar
references are checked; no tolerance or comparison rule is changed.
